# wujs-curated-skills

Use this project-local rule as a bridge to the curated skills in this
repository.

- The canonical skill source is `skills/<bucket>/<skill>/SKILL.md`.
- Use `diagnose` for hard bugs, broken behavior, exceptions, failing tests, or
  performance regressions.
- Use `karpathy-guidelines` for non-trivial code writing, review, or refactoring
  where hidden assumptions, overengineering, broad diffs, or weak verification
  could cause mistakes.
- Use `tdd` when the user asks for test-first development or red-green-refactor.
- Use `zoom-out` when unfamiliar code needs a higher-level map.
- Use `improve-codebase-architecture` for architecture review, refactoring
  opportunities, and deepening shallow modules.
- Use `grill-me` to stress-test a plan or design through one-question-at-a-time
  interrogation.
- Use `shared-server-codex-isolation` (**explicit-only**) when the user invokes
  it for Codex isolation on a shared multi-user host, `codex-wjs` setup, personal
  Codex home placement, or avoiding global default home and shell credential
  leakage.
- Use `shared-server-git-private` (**explicit-only**) when the user invokes it
  for jason-wjs private Git on shared hosts: per-repo local identity, proxy
  discovery per host, or Fine-grained PAT bootstrap and refresh.
- Use `grill-with-docs` to stress-test a plan against `CONTEXT.md`, ADRs, and
  the project's existing domain language.
- Use `write-a-skill` when creating or adapting agent skills.
- Use `bcecmd` when working with Baidu BCE BOS through the `bcecmd` CLI.
- Use `pueue` when managing local single-user long-running shell command queues
  through Pueue/`pueued`.
- Do not copy full skill bodies into Cursor rules; open the relevant `SKILL.md`
  from the repository when needed.
